Define

\deqn{
A_i = Z_i K_i Z_i'.
}

The phenotypic variance-covariance matrix is

\deqn{
V =
\sum_i \sigma_i^2 A_i
+
\sigma_e^2 I.
}

Therefore,

\deqn{
\frac{\partial V}{\partial \sigma_i^2}
=
A_i,
}

and

\deqn{
\frac{\partial V}{\partial \sigma_e^2}
=
I.
}

For REML, the expected Fisher information matrix is calculated as

\deqn{
I_{ab}
=
\frac{1}{2}
\mathrm{tr}(P V_a P V_b),
